    {
      "id": "claim_2bb63455e4bc43e499c3dbb9d5d98f0a",
      "statement": "The Runnable interface is the foundational execution abstraction in LangChain that defines a unified, composable protocol for synchronous invoke, asynchronous invoke, batch processing, streaming, and schema introspection across all LangChain components. The LangChain Expression Language (LCEL) leverages Runnables to enable declarative composition with operators and methods for sequential piping, parallel forking, branching, fallback, and retry logic.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L197-L330",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28391bc12100849c0c4d67024109dcfe286e26296dc8c6b513b743fd84205bba:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_58f09fe58b074804ad7a5757156ef589",
      "statement": "The Runnable abstract base class defines a unified execution interface where invoke is the only abstract method that subclasses must implement; all other execution methods (ainvoke, batch, abatch, stream, astream, transform, atransform) have default implementations that derive from invoke or use thread pool/async executors for parallelism.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L197-L330",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28391bc12100849c0c4d67024109dcfe286e26296dc8c6b513b743fd84205bba:"
