    {
      "id": "claim_43df48a3a6604c3880d84c7f5403db99",
      "statement": "RunnableConfig is a dictionary that threads execution context (tags, metadata, callbacks, max_concurrency, run_name, run_id, configurable) through the entire chain, enabling tracing, concurrency control, lifecycle hooks, and dynamic parameter overrides at any composition point.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L39-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e19505c7353f7c499fd2d63dbcb52bc660faede08e241909e7cb68374679c73c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8575806e92184b30be6df66311523c37",
      "statement": "The batch method uses ThreadPoolExecutor by default for parallelism, calling invoke for each input. Subclasses can override for batching-aware APIs. Single input bypasses executor overhead. Config can be a single RunnableConfig applied to all inputs or a list of configs (one per input). max_concurrency from config limits parallel operations.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L1024-L1043",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4748d5482604acb49da8c80fb6c2d0aef48c054397d59c45eee17144d9843854:"
        },
        {
